Mon Oct 19 09:41:06 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.12.0 (skips 0.11.0, no separate update staged):
  * v0.11.0: MCP search gains full flag (cap 10 to 100); capped
    results report N of M matches; content search walks the whole
    tree with stable results; Rust calls inside macro and
    attribute arguments are found; grok separates tests from
    callers; tilth diff honours custom git config; tree-sitter 0.27
  * v0.12.0: Go type, const and var declarations are definitions
    now; a file passed as scope is an error (was a silent widen
    to root); omitted scope searches root; Go/Rust comment
    markers no longer doubled; /pattern/flags is a regex on CLI;
    tilth_savings tool removed; tilth install learns
    antigravity-cli host; builds clean on Rust 1.99

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Sep 10 17:45:32 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package: tilth 0.10.1, a tree-sitter based code indexer that
  answers structural queries (definitions, references, callers, file
  outlines) from the CLI or as an MCP server instead of dumping whole
  files:
  * vendored crates are updated off upstream's Cargo.lock
    (cargo_vendor update=true), so the shipped binary is not built
    from the exact dependency set upstream tested
  * License: covers the statically linked non-MIT crates -
    Apache-2.0 (tree-sitter-elixir), BSD-3-Clause (encoding_rs),
    Zlib (foldhash)
  * requires git-core at runtime: "tilth diff" and the file overview
    shell out to git

